{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788301109,"nonce":"Xwb3unjhDFofXgeVTlD2Qe5tRCU=","message":"THE FIXTURE THIS ISSUE EXISTS TO CREATE OCCURRED BY ITSELF, so the acceptance bullet it was blocking is already met — but the issue is still worth doing, and for a sharper reason than it currently states.\n\nSession 21, bench `_RimWorld-Agent` `20260901T213125`, `--quicktest`, assembly `1.0.0+cb5de43`. Envelopes at `accept/runs/s21-20260901/posture/`.\n\n## What happened\n\nA bare `--quicktest` map rolled **two violence-incapable colonists out of three**:\n\n    incapable_of_violence: [\n      {pawn: 310, name: \"Danielle\", gate: \"violent-disabled\", …},\n      {pawn: 314, name: \"Greve\",    gate: \"violent-disabled\", …}]\n\nSo `b1b3060`'s \"a pawn incapable of violence is refused by name\" was provable without any gene verb at all, and `digest.posture` read `will_seek 0/1` and `attack 0/1` on a three-colonist colony — the denominators being over violence-capable pawns.\n\n## Why the issue still matters, restated\n\nThe blocking framing in this issue's body is now wrong: the bullet is not blocked, it is **unreliable**. Which is worse in a specific way this issue should say.\n\nA fixture that depends on the roll is a fixture that passes on some maps and SKIPs on others, and `b1b3060`'s suite handles that honestly (batch-rolls up to forty colonists, then `precondition()` → exit 2 with the recipe). But an acceptance bullet whose coverage is decided by world-gen is a bullet nobody can rely on in a regression run — it will be green on the map where it was written and skipped on the next one, and a skip reads like a pass at a glance. That is a stronger argument for `dev:add-gene`/`dev:remove-gene` than \"the fixture cannot be built\", because it survives the observation that sometimes it can.\n\nIt also means the SKIP path in that suite has now probably never been exercised on a map where it fires, and the pass path has. Worth knowing which branch is actually tested.\n\n## Suggested addition to Acceptance\n\n- `dev:add-gene {pawn, def:\"ViolenceDisabled\"}` makes a violence-capable colonist violence-incapable, and `posture` moves that pawn from `accepted` into `incapable_of_violence` with the `violent-disabled` gate, on a map where no colonist rolled that way.\n- The reverse: `dev:remove-gene` restores them, and `digest.posture`'s `will_seek` and `attack` denominators move by one in each direction — proving the denominator is computed rather than cached.\n- The suite's existing batch-roll path is REPLACED by the verb rather than kept as a fallback, so the bullet's coverage stops depending on world-gen. Leaving both means the unreliable path is still the one that runs on most maps.","files":null}]}